<Bindings>
    <!-- Deliberately bare: a name, and a body. Nothing else.

         An earlier version carried a category attribute to push the row into
         the AddOns group of the Key Bindings panel. That attribute is not in
         this client's schema, and WoW does not ignore what it does not know.
         It rejects the whole element: "Bindings.xml:12 Unrecognized XML:
         Binding", and no binding at all. Do not add an attribute here that has
         not been seen working in game.

         No header either. One rendered as the literal string HEADER_EMOTEMENU:
         the panel looks a header's display name up as BINDING_NAME_HEADER_
         plus the header name, not the BINDING_HEADER_ form that every addon
         guide says to define, so the lookup missed and it printed the raw key.
         One binding does not need a heading over it regardless.

         The body runs in the global environment, so it calls a global the
         addon defines rather than anything local to it. The name shown in the
         panel comes from BINDING_NAME_EMOTEMENU_TOGGLE, set alongside it. -->
    <Binding name="EMOTEMENU_TOGGLE">
        EmoteMenu_Toggle()
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
